to do the more advanced version of the scaling laws

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,360
lecture, where we're going to basically go

14
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:46,000
into a bunch of modern, open model tech reports, things

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,165
like mu P and other parameter initializations,

16
00:00:48,165 --> 00:00:50,040
and this year I'm going to throw in some more

17
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:51,060
stuff for optimizers.

18
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,560
So there will be an advanced version

19
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,893
of this that will try to really get to the cutting edge.

20
00:00:54,893 --> 00:00:58,840
Today, we're going to start with all the really basic stuff.

21
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:01,362
And due to some scheduling constraints,

22
